{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NSEjmwt3jfKVD4hBdH2jsX","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→id: test-rel00.0\n     2→title: \"Test Suite: rel00.0 — build lifecycle, cmd/version, pkg/format, pkg/sys, and pkg/testutils\"\n     3→release: rel00.0\n     4→\n     5→traces:\n     6→  - rel00.0-uc001-magefiles\n     7→  - prd011-magefiles R1\n     8→  - prd011-magefiles R2\n     9→  - prd011-magefiles R3\n    10→  - prd011-magefiles R4\n    11→  - rel00.0-uc002-format\n    12→  - prd003-format R1\n    13→  - prd003-format R2\n    14→  - prd003-format R3\n    15→  - rel00.0-uc003-sys\n    16→  - prd002-sys R1\n    17→  - prd002-sys R2\n    18→  - prd002-sys R3\n    19→  - prd002-sys R4\n    20→  - rel00.0-uc004-testutils\n    21→  - prd001-testutils R1\n    22→  - prd001-testutils R2\n    23→  - prd001-testutils R3\n    24→  - prd001-testutils R4\n    25→  - prd001-testutils R5\n    26→\n    27→preconditions:\n    28→  - A git repository with at least one tag matching v[0-9]*.\n    29→  - golangci-lint is installed and on PATH.\n    30→  - mage is installed and on PATH.\n    31→  - configuration.yaml exists at the project root with project.binary_dir set to bin.\n    32→\n    33→test_cases:\n    34→  # --- uc001-magefiles: build lifecycle and version ---\n    35→\n    36→  - name: build_produces_version_binary\n    37→    description: mage build compiles cmd/version to bin/version.\n    38→    inputs:\n    39→      command: \"mage build\"\n    40→    expected:\n    41→      exit_code: 0\n    42→      postcondition: bin/version exists and is executable\n    43→    traces:\n    44→      - prd011-magefiles R2.1\n    45→      - prd011-magefiles R2.4\n    46→\n    47→  - name: version_prints_tag\n    48→    description: bin/version prints the latest version tag and exits 0.\n    49→    inputs:\n    50→      command: \"bin/version\"\n    51→    expected:\n    52→      exit_code: 0\n    53→      stdout_pattern: \"v[0-9]+\\\\.[0-9]+\\\\.[0-9]+\\n\"\n    54→      stderr: \"\"\n    55→    traces:\n    56→      - prd011-magefiles R1.1\n    57→      - prd011-magefiles R1.2\n    58→      - prd011-magefiles R1.3\n    59→\n    60→  - name: version_flag_identical\n    61→    description: bin/version --version produces the same output as bin/version.\n    62→    inputs:\n    63→      command: \"bin/version --version\"\n    64→    expected:\n    65→      exit_code: 0\n    66→      stdout: same as bin/version with no arguments\n    67→      stderr: \"\"\n    68→    traces:\n    69→      - prd011-magefiles R1.4\n    70→\n    71→  - name: version_v_flag_identical\n    72→    description: bin/version -v produces the same output as bin/version.\n    73→    inputs:\n    74→      command: \"bin/version -v\"\n    75→    expected:\n    76→      exit_code: 0\n    77→      stdout: same as bin/version with no arguments\n    78→      stderr: \"\"\n    79→    traces:\n    80→      - prd011-magefiles R1.4\n    81→\n    82→  - name: version_unknown_flag\n    83→    description: bin/version --bogus prints usage to stderr and exits 2.\n    84→    inputs:\n    85→      command: \"bin/version --bogus\"\n    86→    expected:\n    87→      exit_code: 2\n    88→      stdout: \"\"\n    89→      stderr_contains: \"usage\"\n    90→    traces:\n    91→      - prd011-magefiles R1.4\n    92→\n    93→  - name: version_dev_build\n    94→    description: A build without ldflags prints \"dev\".\n    95→    inputs:\n    96→      command: \"go build -o /tmp/version-dev ./cmd/version && /tmp/version-dev\"\n    97→    expected:\n    98→      exit_code: 0\n    99→      stdout: \"dev\\n\"\n   100→      stderr: \"\"\n   101→    traces:\n   102→      - prd011-magefiles R1.2\n   103→\n   104→  - name: lint_passes\n   105→    description: mage lint runs golangci-lint with no warnings.\n   106→    inputs:\n   107→      command: \"mage lint\"\n   108→    expected:\n   109→      exit_code: 0\n   110→    traces:\n   111→      - prd011-magefiles R3.1\n   112→      - prd011-magefiles R3.2\n   113→\n   114→  - name: clean_removes_bin\n   115→    description: mage clean removes the bin/ directory.\n   116→    inputs:\n   117→      command: \"mage build && mage clean\"\n   118→    expected:\n   119→      exit_code: 0\n   120→      postcondition: bin/ does not exist\n   121→    traces:\n   122→      - prd011-magefiles R4.1\n   123→\n   124→  - name: clean_idempotent\n   125→    description: mage clean succeeds when bin/ does not exist.\n   126→    inputs:\n   127→      command: \"mage clean && mage clean\"\n   128→    expected:\n   129→      exit_code: 0\n   130→    traces:\n   131→      - prd011-magefiles R4.1\n   132→\n   133→  # --- uc002-format: pkg/format output formatting ---\n   134→\n   135→  - name: columns_20_entries_80_width\n   136→    description: Columns distributes 20 filenames into a grid fitting 80 columns.\n   137→    inputs:\n   138→      function: \"format.Columns(entries, 80)\"\n   139→      entries: 20 filenames of varying lengths\n   140→    expected:\n   141→      postcondition: each row fits within 80 characters; column count is maximized\n   142→    traces:\n   143→      - prd003-format R1.1\n   144→      - prd003-format R1.4\n   145→\n   146→  - name: columns_empty_input\n   147→    description: Columns returns nil for empty input.\n   148→    inputs:\n   149→      function: \"format.Columns(nil, 80)\"\n   150→    expected:\n   151→      result: nil\n   152→    traces:\n   153→      - prd003-format R1.1\n   154→\n   155→  - name: pad_right\n   156→    description: PadRight pads a string with trailing spaces to the specified width.\n   157→    inputs:\n   158→      function: 'format.PadRight(\"abc\", 10)'\n   159→    expected:\n   160→      result: '\"abc       \"  (abc + 7 spaces)'\n   161→    traces:\n   162→      - prd003-format R1.2\n   163→\n   164→  - name: pad_left\n   165→    description: PadLeft pads a string with leading spaces to the specified width.\n   166→    inputs:\n   167→      function: 'format.PadLeft(\"abc\", 10)'\n   168→    expected:\n   169→      result: '\"       abc\"  (7 spaces + abc)'\n   170→    traces:\n   171→      - prd003-format R1.2\n   172→\n   173→  - name: display_width_multibyte\n   174→    description: Column width uses rune count, not byte count, for multi-byte strings.\n   175→    inputs:\n   176→      function: 'format.PadRight(\"café\", 10)'\n   177→    expected:\n   178→      result: '\"café      \"  (café is 4 runes, padded to 10)'\n   179→    traces:\n   180→      - prd003-format R1.3\n   181→\n   182→  - name: file_type_color_all_types\n   183→    description: FileTypeColor returns correct ANSI codes for all eight file types.\n   184→    inputs:\n   185→      function: \"format.FileTypeColor(mode) for each file type\"\n   186→      setup: \"format.SetColorEnabled(true)\"\n   187→    expected:\n   188→      directory: '\"\\033[34m\"'\n   189→      symlink: '\"\\033[36m\"'\n   190→      executable: '\"\\033[32m\"'\n   191→      block_device: '\"\\033[33;1m\"'\n   192→      char_device: '\"\\033[33;1m\"'\n   193→      socket: '\"\\033[35m\"'\n   194→      pipe: '\"\\033[33m\"'\n   195→      regular: '\"\"'\n   196→    traces:\n   197→      - prd003-format R2.1\n   198→      - prd003-format R2.4\n   199→\n   200→  - name: reset_color_enabled\n   201→    description: Reset returns ANSI reset sequence when color is enabled.\n   202→    inputs:\n   203→      function: \"format.Reset()\"\n   204→      setup: \"format.SetColorEnabled(true)\"\n   205→    expected:\n   206→      result: '\"\\033[0m\"'\n   207→    traces:\n   208→      - prd003-format R2.2\n   209→\n   210→  - name: color_disabled_suppresses_output\n   211→    description: SetColorEnabled(false) causes FileTypeColor and Reset to return empty strings.\n   212→    inputs:\n   213→      function: \"format.FileTypeColor(os.ModeDir) and format.Reset()\"\n   214→      setup: \"format.SetColorEnabled(false)\"\n   215→    expected:\n   216→      file_type_color: '\"\"'\n   217→      reset: '\"\"'\n   218→    traces:\n   219→      - prd003-format R2.6\n   220→\n   221→  - name: reset_color_enabled_restores_auto\n   222→    description: ResetColorEnabled clears the override and reverts to TTY detection.\n   223→    inputs:\n   224→      function: \"format.ResetColorEnabled() then format.ColorEnabled(pipe)\"\n   225→      setup: \"format.SetColorEnabled(true); format.ResetColorEnabled()\"\n   226→    expected:\n   227→      color_enabled_pipe: false\n   228→    traces:\n   229→      - prd003-format R2.7\n   230→\n   231→  - name: color_enabled_pipe\n   232→    description: ColorEnabled returns false for an os.Pipe writer.\n   233→    inputs:\n   234→      function: \"format.ColorEnabled(pipeWriter)\"\n   235→    expected:\n   236→      result: false\n   237→    traces:\n   238→      - prd003-format R2.3\n   239→\n   240→  - name: color_enabled_non_file\n   241→    description: ColorEnabled returns false for a bytes.Buffer (non-*os.File).\n   242→    inputs:\n   243→      function: \"format.ColorEnabled(&bytes.Buffer{})\"\n   244→    expected:\n   245→      result: false\n   246→    traces:\n   247→      - prd003-format R2.3\n   248→\n   249→  - name: human_size_binary\n   250→    description: HumanSize converts bytes using 1024-based units.\n   251→    inputs:\n   252→      function: \"format.HumanSize(1536, HumanSizeOpts{Binary: true})\"\n   253→    expected:\n   254→      result: '\"1.5K\"'\n   255→    traces:\n   256→      - prd003-format R3.1\n   257→      - prd003-format R3.2\n   258→      - prd003-format R3.3\n   259→\n   260→  - name: human_size_si\n   261→    description: HumanSize converts bytes using 1000-based SI units.\n   262→    inputs:\n   263→      function: \"format.HumanSize(1000000, HumanSizeOpts{Binary: false})\"\n   264→    expected:\n   265→      result: '\"1.0MB\"'\n   266→    traces:\n   267→      - prd003-format R3.1\n   268→      - prd003-format R3.2\n   269→\n   270→  - name: human_size_zero\n   271→    description: HumanSize returns \"0\" for zero bytes.\n   272→    inputs:\n   273→      function: \"format.HumanSize(0, HumanSizeOpts{Binary: true})\"\n   274→    expected:\n   275→      result: '\"0\"'\n   276→    traces:\n   277→      - prd003-format R3.4\n   278→\n   279→  # --- uc003-sys: pkg/sys syscall abstractions ---\n   280→\n   281→  - name: terminal_width_pipe\n   282→    description: TerminalWidth returns an error when stdout is a pipe.\n   283→    inputs:\n   284→      function: \"sys.TerminalWidth() with stdout redirected to a pipe\"\n   285→    expected:\n   286→      error: non-nil\n   287→    traces:\n   288→      - prd002-sys R1.1\n   289→\n   290→  - name: is_terminal_pipe_fd\n   291→    description: IsTerminal returns false for a pipe file descriptor.\n   292→    inputs:\n   293→      function: \"sys.IsTerminal(pipeFd)\"\n   294→    expected:\n   295→      result: false\n   296→    traces:\n   297→      - prd002-sys R1.3\n   298→\n   299→  - name: stat_known_file\n   300→    description: Stat returns correct extended metadata for a known file.\n   301→    inputs:\n   302→      function: \"sys.Stat(testFile)\"\n   303→    expected:\n   304→      postcondition: Nlink, Uid, Gid, Dev, Ino, Blocks match stat(1) output\n   305→    traces:\n   306→      - prd002-sys R2.1\n   307→      - prd002-sys R2.2\n   308→\n   309→  - name: lstat_symlink\n   310→    description: Lstat on a symlink returns symlink type bits, not target's mode.\n   311→    inputs:\n   312→      function: \"sys.Lstat(symlinkPath)\"\n   313→    expected:\n   314→      postcondition: \"Mode & os.ModeSymlink != 0\"\n   315→    traces:\n   316→      - prd002-sys R2.1\n   317→\n   318→  - name: stat_modtime_populated\n   319→    description: Stat returns a non-zero ModTime from the platform-correct field.\n   320→    inputs:\n   321→      function: \"sys.Stat(testFile)\"\n   322→    expected:\n   323→      postcondition: ModTime is non-zero and close to os.Stat(testFile).ModTime()\n   324→    traces:\n   325→      - prd002-sys R2.3\n   326→\n   327→  - name: stat_hard_link_count\n   328→    description: Stat returns correct Nlink for a file with multiple hard links.\n   329→    inputs:\n   330→      setup: \"create testFile, create hard link to testFile\"\n   331→      function: \"sys.Stat(testFile)\"\n   332→    expected:\n   333→      postcondition: Nlink == 2\n   334→    traces:\n   335→      - prd002-sys R2.2\n   336→\n   337→  - name: sigpipe_handler_exit_zero\n   338→    description: InstallSIGPIPEHandler causes exit 0 on broken pipe.\n   339→    inputs:\n   340→      function: \"sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() then write to closed pipe\"\n   341→    expected:\n   342→      exit_code: 0\n   343→    traces:\n   344→      - prd002-sys R3.1\n   345→\n   346→  - name: on_terminal_resize_callback\n   347→    description: OnTerminalResize registers a callback invoked on SIGWINCH.\n   348→    inputs:\n   349→      function: \"sys.OnTerminalResize(callback) then send SIGWINCH\"\n   350→    expected:\n   351→      postcondition: callback was called with a positive width\n   352→    traces:\n   353→      - prd002-sys R4.1\n   354→      - prd002-sys R4.2\n   355→\n   356→  - name: cross_platform_compile\n   357→    description: All pkg/sys code compiles on darwin/arm64 and linux/amd64.\n   358→    inputs:\n   359→      command: \"GOOS=darwin GOARCH=arm64 go build ./pkg/sys/ && GOOS=linux GOARCH=amd64 go build ./pkg/sys/\"\n   360→    expected:\n   361→      exit_code: 0\n   362→    traces:\n   363→      - prd002-sys R1.2\n   364→\n   365→  # --- uc004-testutils: pkg/testutils differential testing harness ---\n   366→\n   367→  - name: difftest_zero_value\n   368→    description: DiffTest zero value is a valid test case that runs without error.\n   369→    inputs:\n   370→      function: \"testutils.RunDiffTests(t, echoBin, echoBin, []DiffTest{{Name: \\\"zero\\\"}})\"\n   371→    expected:\n   372→      postcondition: test passes with no output\n   373→    